## Recommendation

- Keep the amount-specific hold of {{ s.hold_amount }}; do not freeze the account and do not escalate [SOP-9-1] [SOP-5-IX].
- Do not file an STR on this account on the present facts; re-assess if new information emerges.
- Advise the holder to file a grievance with documents that support the credit (for example a rent agreement or an invoice) [SOP-10-1].
- Complete enhanced due diligence (KYC refresh, source of the credit, relationship with the remitter) and record the outcome on CFCFRMS [SOP-10-1].

## Timelines [SOP-10-1]

- Grievance by the holder: within 7 days.
- Decision on the grievance by the Investigating Officer: within 15 days.
- Escalation to the DGO if unresolved: within 15 days.
- Lapse of the hold: after 90 days unless continued; intimate the Law Enforcement Agency before the lapse (around day 75).
